title: Charts in the game
intro: A Chart draws a line or bar graph for the HUD or the world. It samples an output with no code, or a script feeds it.
project: Empty | Factory Chart
write: Scripts/Factory.cs | runtime-chart/Factory.cs
write: Scripts/Backlog.cs | runtime-chart/Backlog.cs

chapter: A chart that samples an output | Entity > UI > Chart
create: Empty
rename: Factory
add: Factory
say: This factory is a stand-in script. Its Cards An Hour output rises and falls as the shifts come and go.
create: Chart
rename: Throughput
set: Transform.Position = 0, 0, 0
look: 0, 0, 3
explain: scene | A chart | Entity, UI, Chart makes a line graph, sized like a bar, with lines across for the values, their numbers, and a legend.
editorset: Chart.Series:name:1 = Cards
editorset: Chart.Series:output:1 = CardsAnHour
set: Chart.Track = Factory
expectvalue: Throughput.Chart.Track = Factory
explain: field:Chart.Series | Series | Each series is a name and a color. Give it an output after the equals sign, and the chart samples it with no code.
explain: field:Chart.Track | Track | Track names the entity whose outputs it samples.
set: Chart.SampleEvery = 0.25
set: Chart.Keep = 40
expectvalue: Throughput.Chart.Keep = 40
explain: field:Chart.SampleEvery | Sample Every | It takes a point every quarter of a second of game time, so a sped up game fills it faster, and keeps the last forty, so the line scrolls.
play
wait: 6
say: The line follows the factory. Its range fits the highest point, rounded up to a round number, and the numbers are written short.
stop

chapter: Fed by a script | chart.Add
select: Throughput
add: Backlog
code: Assets/Scripts/Backlog.cs | Backlog.cs
say: A script adds points itself, with Add and a series' name. A name no row has gets a series of its own, in the next color.
click: editor:Chart.XLabels:add
editorset: Chart.XLabels:item:1 = 10 seconds ago
click: editor:Chart.XLabels:add
editorset: Chart.XLabels:item:2 = Now
explain: field:Chart.XLabels | X Labels | X Labels are words spread along the bottom, from the left end to the right.
play
wait: 6
say: Two series now, each in its own color and named in the legend.
stop

chapter: Bars | Kind
set: Chart.Kind = Bars
set: Chart.Keep = 12
set: Chart.SampleEvery = 1
expectvalue: Throughput.Chart.Kind = Bars
explain: field:Chart.Kind | Kind | Kind Bars draws a bar for each point instead, the series side by side.
play
wait: 6
say: Set Max to fix the range, and Format to write the numbers your way. A rewind puts the points back, and in a network game the host's points are sent to everyone.
stop
